claimed: script-temp-tests-watch-a-shared-directory -- fix the false-alarm found 2026-09-04. TestScalaScript.'run: leaves no temp file/directory behind' and TestPage.'close() deletes the cached compiled program's temp output directory' both snapshot the SHARED java.io.tmpdir for okay-script-* entries before/after and assert equality; a sibling worktree's own okay-script tests running concurrently create matching entries between the two snapshots and fail the assertion for a reason that has nothing to do with this code's own cleanup. Fix: give each test its own temp ROOT (a fresh directory passed to the code under test via a system property or a parameter, not the shared java.io.tmpdir) and snapshot THAT -- keeps the real property (this code cleans up after itself) while dropping the false alarm from watching a directory the whole machine shares. ScalaScript.compileOnly currently hardcodes Files.createTempDirectory("okay-script-") against the system default tmp dir; needs a way to override the parent dir for tests.
